menu "Lab 4 two-point calibration constants"

    config LAB4_CAL_GAIN_PPM
        int "Calibration gain correction, in ppm (1000000 = x1.000)"
        default 970874
        help
            Multiplicative correction applied to a raw ADC code (after the
            offset correction below) to cancel out the ADC/sensor's known
            gain error, expressed in parts per million so it can be an
            integer Kconfig value: corrected = raw_after_offset * PPM/1e6.

            The default, 970874 (= round(1e6 / 1.03)), exactly cancels
            adc_sim's synthetic x1.03 gain error (see
            labs/common/components/adc_sim/README.md) -- on the real
            adc_oneshot path, re-derive this from two known reference
            voltages (two-point calibration) instead of trusting the
            default, which is sim-specific.

    config LAB4_CAL_OFFSET
        int "Calibration offset correction, in raw LSB"
        default 25
        help
            Subtracted from the raw ADC code before the gain correction
            above: corrected = (raw - OFFSET) * PPM/1e6.

            The default, 25, exactly cancels adc_sim's synthetic +25 LSB
            offset error (see labs/common/components/adc_sim/README.md) --
            on the real adc_oneshot path, re-derive this from two known
            reference voltages instead of trusting the default, which is
            sim-specific.

endmenu
